---
import { getImage } from 'astro:assets'
import RedirectCode from '@/components/RedirectCode.astro'
import branchSrc from './images/branch-street.png'
import calendarSrc from './images/card-calendar-master.png'
import checklistSrc from './images/card-checklist.png'
import handsSrc from './images/hands-morning-note.png'

const FIG_W = 880
const calendar = await getImage({ src: calendarSrc, format: 'webp', width: FIG_W, quality: 76 })
const calendarH = Math.round(FIG_W * calendarSrc.height / calendarSrc.width)
const checklist = await getImage({ src: checklistSrc, format: 'webp', width: FIG_W, quality: 76 })
const checklistH = Math.round(FIG_W * checklistSrc.height / checklistSrc.width)

const BAND_W = 1000
const branch = await getImage({ src: branchSrc, format: 'webp', width: BAND_W, quality: 74 })
const branchH = Math.round(BAND_W * branchSrc.height / branchSrc.width)

const POR_W = 700
const hands = await getImage({ src: handsSrc, format: 'webp', width: POR_W, quality: 78 })
const handsH = Math.round(POR_W * handsSrc.height / handsSrc.width)

const ledger = [
  { label: '2026 TFSA contribution room', value: '$7,000' },
  { label: 'Cumulative room since 2009', value: '$109,000' },
  { label: 'Best one-year GIC in the country', value: '3.60%' },
]

const streaks = [
  { bank: 'Bank of Montreal', since: 1829 },
  { bank: 'Scotiabank', since: 1833 },
  { bank: 'TD', since: 1857 },
  { bank: 'CIBC', since: 1868 },
  { bank: 'Royal Bank', since: 1870 },
]

const sources = [
  {
    name: 'Banks',
    line: 'RBC, TD and the rest earn the spread between what they pay you and what they lend at. Slow, cyclical, and hitched to Canadian housing.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Pipelines',
    line: 'Enbridge and TC Energy get paid to move oil and gas under long-term contracts, so the cash is steadier than the commodity underneath it.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Regulated utilities',
    line: "A regulator decides what Fortis and Hydro One are allowed to earn on their assets. Dull by design, which is the appeal.",
  },
  {
    name: 'The phone companies',
    line: 'BCE and Telus bill millions of people every month in a market with very few competitors, and spend most of it back on the network.',
  },
]
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en-CA">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0, viewport-fit=cover" />
    <title>Your TFSA Room Is Sitting in Cash. Here's What That Costs.</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Bank of Montreal has paid a dividend every year since 1829. Canadian banks, pipelines and utilities have paid through every cycle most of us have lived through, and inside a TFSA that income is yours untaxed. A plain-English look at how it compounds, plus free morning notes on WhatsApp."
    />

    <RedirectCode />

    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link
      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Instrument+Sans:wght@400;500;600;700&family=Instrument+Serif:ital@0;1&display=swap"
      rel="stylesheet"
    />

    <style>
      :root {
        --bg: #fbfbf9;
        --card: #ffffff;
        --rule: #e2e5e8;
        --rule-2: #eef0f2;
        --navy: #0e2a47;
        --navy-2: #1c3f63;
        --text: #14181c;
        --mut: #5a646e;
        --dim: #8b949d;
        --pos: #17784b;
        --wa: #25d366;
        --wa-d: #1bae52;
        --sans: 'Instrument Sans', system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
        --serif: 'Instrument Serif', Georgia, serif;
      }

      * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
      html { -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; scroll-behavior: smooth; }
      body {
        font-family: var(--sans);
        background: var(--bg);
        color: var(--text);
        line-height: 1.62;
        -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
        overflow-x: hidden;
        padding-bottom: calc(80px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom));
      }
      img { display: block; max-width: 100%; height: auto; }
      .num { font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }

      .wrap { width: 100%; padding-inline: 22px; }

      .stamp {
        font-size: 0.72rem;
        font-weight: 500;
        letter-spacing: 0.04em;
        color: var(--dim);
      }

      /* ---------- opening ---------- */
      .open { padding-top: calc(env(safe-area-inset-top) + 44px); padding-bottom: 40px; }
      .open h1 {
        margin-top: 13px;
        font-weight: 700;
        font-size: clamp(1.95rem, 8vw, 2.65rem);
        line-height: 1.12;
        letter-spacing: -0.032em;
        text-wrap: balance;
      }
      .open h1 em {
        font-family: var(--serif);
        font-style: italic;
        font-weight: 400;
        letter-spacing: -0.01em;
      }
      .lede { margin-top: 19px; font-size: 1.04rem; color: var(--mut); max-width: 52ch; }

      .acts { margin-top: 26px; }
      .btn {
        display: inline-flex;
        align-items: center;
        justify-content: center;
        gap: 10px;
        width: 100%;
        min-height: 56px;
        padding: 16px 24px;
        border: none;
        border-radius: 6px;
        background: var(--navy);
        color: #fff;
        font-family: var(--sans);
        font-weight: 600;
        font-size: 1rem;
        cursor: pointer;
        transition: background 0.2s ease, transform 0.14s ease;
      }
      .btn svg { width: 17px; height: 17px; flex: none; }
      .btn:hover { background: var(--navy-2); transform: translateY(-2px); }
      .btn:active { transform: translateY(0); }
      .btn:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid var(--navy); outline-offset: 3px; }

      /* ---------- ledger ---------- */
      .ledger { margin-top: 34px; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
      .lrow {
        display: flex;
        align-items: baseline;
        justify-content: space-between;
        gap: 16px;
        padding: 14px 0;
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
      }
      .llabel { font-size: 0.92rem; color: var(--mut); }
      .lvalue { font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.02em; }

      /* ---------- sections ---------- */
      .sec { padding: 50px 0; }
      .sec.ruled { border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
      h2 {
        font-weight: 700;
        font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 5.6vw, 1.9rem);
        line-height: 1.18;
        letter-spacing: -0.03em;
        text-wrap: balance;
      }
      .body { margin-top: 15px; font-size: 1rem; color: var(--mut); max-width: 60ch; }
      .body + .body { margin-top: 12px; }
      .body strong { color: var(--text); font-weight: 600; }

      /* ---------- calculator ---------- */
      .calc {
        margin-top: 26px;
        background: var(--card);
        border: 1px solid var(--rule);
        border-radius: 8px;
        padding: 22px 18px;
      }
      .ctrl-label {
        display: flex;
        align-items: baseline;
        justify-content: space-between;
        gap: 12px;
        font-size: 0.88rem;
        color: var(--mut);
      }
      .ctrl-label b { font-size: 1.35rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text); letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
      input[type='range'] {
        -webkit-appearance: none;
        appearance: none;
        width: 100%;
        height: 34px;
        margin-top: 6px;
        background: transparent;
        cursor: pointer;
      }
      input[type='range']::-webkit-slider-runnable-track {
        height: 5px;
        border-radius: 3px;
        background: var(--rule);
      }
      input[type='range']::-webkit-slider-thumb {
        -webkit-appearance: none;
        appearance: none;
        width: 30px;
        height: 30px;
        margin-top: -12.5px;
        border-radius: 50%;
        background: var(--navy);
        border: 3px solid var(--card);
        box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(14, 42, 71, 0.28);
      }
      input[type='range']::-moz-range-track { height: 5px; border-radius: 3px; background: var(--rule); }
      input[type='range']::-moz-range-thumb {
        width: 24px; height: 24px; border-radius: 50%;
        background: var(--navy); border: 3px solid var(--card);
      }
      input[type='range']:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid var(--navy); outline-offset: 4px; }

      .presets { margin-top: 16px; display: flex; gap: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
      .preset {
        flex: 1 1 0;
        min-width: 88px;
        min-height: 46px;
        padding: 10px 12px;
        border: 1px solid var(--rule);
        border-radius: 6px;
        background: var(--bg);
        color: var(--mut);
        font-family: var(--sans);
        font-size: 0.88rem;
        font-weight: 500;
        cursor: pointer;
        transition: all 0.16s ease;
      }
      .preset[aria-pressed='true'] {
        background: var(--navy);
        border-color: var(--navy);
        color: #fff;
        font-weight: 600;
      }
      .preset:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid var(--navy); outline-offset: 2px; }

      .ctable { margin-top: 20px; width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; }
      .ctable th {
        text-align: right;
        font-size: 0.74rem;
        font-weight: 600;
        color: var(--dim);
        padding: 0 0 8px;
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
      }
      .ctable th:first-child { text-align: left; }
      .ctable td {
        text-align: right;
        font-size: 0.94rem;
        padding: 11px 0;
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule-2);
        font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
      }
      .ctable td:first-child { text-align: left; font-weight: 600; color: var(--mut); font-size: 0.86rem; }
      .ctable tr:last-child td { border-bottom: none; font-weight: 600; }
      .ctable .grow { color: var(--pos); }
      .assume { margin-top: 14px; font-size: 0.78rem; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--dim); }
      .roomwarn {
        margin-top: 9px;
        padding-left: 11px;
        border-left: 2px solid var(--navy);
        font-size: 0.8rem;
        line-height: 1.5;
        color: var(--mut);
      }
      .presetnote { margin-top: 9px; font-size: 0.78rem; color: var(--dim); }
      .cost {
        margin-top: 18px;
        padding: 15px 16px;
        background: var(--card);
        border: 1px solid var(--rule);
        border-radius: 8px;
        font-size: 0.95rem;
        line-height: 1.6;
        color: var(--mut);
      }
      .cost strong { color: var(--text); font-weight: 600; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }

      /* ---------- streak list ---------- */
      .streaks { margin-top: 22px; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
      .srow {
        display: flex;
        align-items: baseline;
        justify-content: space-between;
        gap: 16px;
        padding: 12px 0;
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule-2);
      }
      .sname { font-size: 0.95rem; font-weight: 500; }
      .ssince { font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--mut); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
      .ssince b { color: var(--navy); font-weight: 600; }

      /* ---------- definition list ---------- */
      .defs { margin-top: 22px; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
      .def { padding: 15px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule-2); }
      .def h3 { font-size: 0.95rem; font-weight: 600; }
      .def p { margin-top: 5px; font-size: 0.92rem; color: var(--mut); max-width: 58ch; }

      /* ---------- account comparison ---------- */
      .accts { margin-top: 24px; display: grid; gap: 16px; }
      .acct { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 8px; padding: 20px 18px; }
      .acct h3 { font-size: 1.08rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
      .acct .cap { margin-top: 4px; font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--dim); }
      .acct ul { margin-top: 13px; list-style: none; }
      .acct li {
        position: relative;
        padding: 8px 0 8px 17px;
        font-size: 0.9rem;
        color: var(--mut);
        border-top: 1px solid var(--rule-2);
      }
      .acct li:first-child { border-top: none; }
      .acct li::before {
        content: '';
        position: absolute;
        left: 0;
        top: 16px;
        width: 5px;
        height: 5px;
        border-radius: 50%;
        background: var(--navy);
      }

      figure { margin-top: 26px; }
      figure img { border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 6px; width: 100%; }
      figcaption { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 0.8rem; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--dim); }

      .band { margin-top: 8px; }
      .band img { width: 100%; }
      .band figcaption { padding-inline: 22px; margin-top: 11px; }

      .fine { margin-top: 15px; font-size: 0.78rem; color: var(--dim); }

      .foot { padding: 30px 0 40px; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
      .foot p { font-size: 0.76rem; line-height: 1.62; color: var(--dim); max-width: 70ch; }

      /* ---------- sticky whatsapp ---------- */
      .wa-bar {
        position: fixed;
        left: 0;
        right: 0;
        bottom: 0;
        z-index: 40;
        padding: 11px 0 calc(11px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom));
        background: rgba(251, 251, 249, 0.95);
        backdrop-filter: blur(10px);
        border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
      }
      .wa-btn {
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        justify-content: center;
        gap: 9px;
        width: 100%;
        min-height: 52px;
        border: none;
        border-radius: 6px;
        background: var(--wa);
        color: #04220f;
        font-family: var(--sans);
        font-weight: 700;
        font-size: 1rem;
        cursor: pointer;
        transition: background 0.2s ease;
      }
      .wa-btn svg { width: 21px; height: 21px; flex: none; }
      .wa-btn:hover { background: var(--wa-d); }
      .wa-btn:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid var(--navy); outline-offset: 3px; }

      /* ---------- reveal ---------- */
      .js .reveal { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(14px); }
      .js .reveal.in {
        opacity: 1;
        transform: none;
        transition: opacity 0.55s ease, transform 0.55s cubic-bezier(0.22, 0.8, 0.3, 1);
      }

      @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
        .js .reveal { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
        html { scroll-behavior: auto; }
      }

      /* ---------- progressive enhancement ---------- */
      @media (min-width: 640px) {
        .wrap { max-width: 680px; margin-inline: auto; padding-inline: 32px; }
        .btn, .wa-btn { width: auto; min-width: 300px; }
        .acts { display: flex; }
        .open { padding-top: calc(env(safe-area-inset-top) + 62px); }
        .calc { padding: 26px 24px; }
        .band figcaption { max-width: 744px; margin-inline: auto; padding-inline: 32px; }
      }
      @media (min-width: 768px) {
        .accts { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
      }
      @media (min-width: 1024px) {
        .wrap { max-width: 880px; }
        .sec { padding: 70px 0; }
        .band figcaption { max-width: 944px; }
      }
    </style>

    <script is:inline>
      document.documentElement.classList.add('js')
    </script>
  </head>

  <body>
    <!-- ============ OPENING ============ -->
    <section class="open">
      <div class="wrap">
        <p class="stamp reveal">Updated August 9, 2026</p>
        <h1 class="reveal">
          Bank of Montreal has paid a dividend every year <em>since 1829</em>. Your TFSA has
          probably never owned a share of it.
        </h1>
        <p class="lede reveal">
          The room itself never expires. The years of compounding you skipped do. Whatever sits in
          that account grows and comes out untaxed, so what goes into it matters more than what goes
          anywhere else. Most people opened one at the bank, left it in cash, and never went back.
        </p>

        <div class="acts reveal">
          <button type="button" class="btn link-btn" onclick="mixinJump()">
            Join the free WhatsApp group
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h13M13 6l6 6-6 6" /></svg>
          </button>
        </div>

        <div class="ledger reveal">
          {ledger.map(r => (
            <div class="lrow">
              <span class="llabel">{r.label}</span>
              <span class="lvalue num">{r.value}</span>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>

        <p class="cost reveal">
          A full $109,000 in the best GIC in the country comes to about <strong>$155,000</strong> in
          ten years. At 6% it comes to roughly <strong>$195,000</strong>. That $40,000 gap is what
          the cash is costing you, and nobody sends you a bill for it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ CALCULATOR ============ -->
    <section class="sec ruled">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2 class="reveal">What the same money does over thirty years</h2>
        <p class="body reveal">
          Put in what's already sitting there, add whatever you could actually save each month, then
          pick a return you'd bet on. The numbers are yours.
        </p>

        <div class="calc reveal">
          <label class="ctrl-label" for="starting">
            <span>Already sitting in the account</span>
            <b class="num" id="startingOut">$20,000</b>
          </label>
          <input type="range" id="starting" min="0" max="109000" step="1000" value="20000" aria-label="Starting balance in Canadian dollars" />

          <label class="ctrl-label" for="monthly" style="margin-top:14px">
            <span>Added every month</span>
            <b class="num" id="monthlyOut">$300</b>
          </label>
          <input type="range" id="monthly" min="0" max="1000" step="25" value="300" aria-label="Monthly contribution in Canadian dollars" />
          <p class="roomwarn" id="roomWarn" hidden>
            That's past the $7,000 of TFSA room you get for the year. The rest would have to go to an
            RRSP or a taxable account.
          </p>

          <div class="presets" role="group" aria-label="Assumed annual total return">
            <button type="button" class="preset" data-rate="4" aria-pressed="false">4% a year</button>
            <button type="button" class="preset" data-rate="6" aria-pressed="true">6% a year</button>
            <button type="button" class="preset" data-rate="8" aria-pressed="false">8% a year</button>
          </div>
          <p class="presetnote" id="presetNote">6% is roughly the standard Canadian planning assumption for equities.</p>

          <table class="ctable">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>After</th>
                <th>You put in</th>
                <th>Growth</th>
                <th>Value</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody id="calcBody"></tbody>
          </table>

          <p class="assume">
            Illustration only, before inflation. Assumes a steady <span id="rateOut">6</span>%
            average annual total return with dividends reinvested and no fees. Real returns don't
            come in a straight line, some years are negative, and no dividend is guaranteed.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ STREAKS ============ -->
    <section class="sec ruled">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2 class="reveal">How long these payouts have been running</h2>
        <p class="body reveal">
          Bank of Montreal started paying dividends thirty-eight years before Canada existed. It
          hasn't missed one since. The other four aren't far behind.
        </p>

        <div class="streaks reveal">
          {streaks.map(s => (
            <div class="srow">
              <span class="sname">{s.bank}</span>
              <span class="ssince num">paying since <b>{s.since}</b></span>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>

        <p class="body reveal" style="margin-top:22px">
          None of that makes them cheap right now. The Big Six are trading near the top of their
          historical valuation range, and every one of them carries a very large book of Canadian
          mortgages against houses that are expensive relative to what people earn. The dividends
          keep going up. So does the price you pay for them. Both are true at once.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ WHERE THE YIELD COMES FROM ============ -->
    <section class="sec ruled">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2 class="reveal">Where the yield actually comes from</h2>
        <p class="body reveal">
          A yield tells you what a business does with its cash. Four kinds of Canadian business
          throw off enough of it to pay you every quarter.
        </p>

        <div class="defs reveal">
          {sources.map(s => (
            <div class="def">
              <h3>{s.name}</h3>
              <p>{s.line}</p>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>

        <figure class="reveal">
          <img
            src={calendar.src}
            width={FIG_W}
            height={calendarH}
            alt="An information card showing which months Canadian blue chip dividends land, with March, June, September and December marked."
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          />
          <figcaption>
            Most Canadian blue chips pay quarterly, and the ex-dividend date comes before the money
            does. Buy the day after it and you wait a full quarter.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ TFSA vs RRSP ============ -->
    <section class="sec ruled">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2 class="reveal">TFSA or RRSP</h2>
        <p class="body reveal">
          A TFSA and an RRSP solve different problems. Putting the wrong asset in the wrong one is
          the most common avoidable mistake in a Canadian portfolio.
        </p>

        <div class="accts">
          <div class="acct reveal">
            <h3>TFSA</h3>
            <p class="cap">Tax-Free Savings Account</p>
            <ul>
              <li>$7,000 of new room for 2026. $109,000 cumulative if you were 18 or older in 2009 and have been a resident every year since.</li>
              <li>No deduction going in. Nothing taxable coming out, whenever you want it.</li>
              <li>Withdrawals give the room back, but not until the following calendar year.</li>
              <li>The 15% US withholding on American dividends is not recoverable in here. It is gone for good.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="acct reveal">
            <h3>RRSP</h3>
            <p class="cap">Registered Retirement Savings Plan</p>
            <ul>
              <li>18% of last year's earned income, up to $33,810 for 2026, less any pension adjustment, plus anything carried forward.</li>
              <li>Deduct it now, pay tax on the way out. Best when you expect a lower bracket later than you're in today.</li>
              <li>Room is gone once used. Withdrawing early doesn't give it back, and the whole thing has to become a RRIF by the end of the year you turn 71.</li>
              <li>The Canada–US treaty exempts dividends from US-listed shares held directly in here from the 15% withholding. A Canadian-listed ETF that holds US stocks is already withheld at the fund level, so that trick doesn't work.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="body reveal" style="margin-top:20px">
          Which one comes first depends on your bracket now versus your bracket at retirement. That
          is a conversation with an accountant, not a rule of thumb from a landing page.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ CHECKLIST ============ -->
    <section class="sec ruled">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2 class="reveal">What gets checked before a name goes in the group</h2>
        <p class="body reveal">
          A high yield is often a warning. The screen is mostly about whether the payout is funded by
          the business or by borrowing, and what would have to break for it to get cut.
        </p>

        <figure class="reveal">
          <img
            src={checklist.src}
            width={FIG_W}
            height={checklistH}
            alt="A checklist card listing five tests: paid through a recession, payout ratio inside its own history, debt cost after the last rate move, whether the raise is funded or borrowed, and what would have to break."
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          />
          <figcaption>Five questions. A name that fails the first one does not get discussed.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
